ighthouse","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":17.901061,"lo":-62.851533,"d":455,"ds":"The Gustavia Lighthouse is a 20th-century lighthouse located in Gustavia, the capital of Saint Barthélemy in the French West Indies. It was constructed in 1961 on the grounds of Fort Gustav, overlooking the Gustavia harbor. Today the lighthouse is a popular location for tourists, hikers, and photographers, as well as a site for viewing regattas, such as the St Barths Bucket Regatta.","wpu":"Gustavia Lighthouse","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9d/Gustaviaphare2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Publique, Saint Barthélemy","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":17.903333,"lo":-62.851389,"d":705,"ds":"Public (French pronunciation: [pyblik] ) is a quartier of Saint Barthélemy in the Caribbean. In the western part of the island, situated 180 km to the North-West of St.John's, around 90 km North-West from the St. Kitts and Nevis border.","wpu":"Publique, Saint Barthélemy","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Saint-Barth%C3%A9lemy_quartiers_map.svg/960px-Saint-Barth%C3%A9lemy_quartiers_map.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Corossol","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":17.908333,"lo":-62.856111,"d":1371,"ds":"Corossol (French pronunciation: [kɔʁɔsɔl]) is a quartier of Saint Barthélemy in the Caribbean. It is located in the northwestern part of the island. The quartiers' language is Norman.","wpu":"Corossol","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Saint-Barth%C3%A9lemy_quartiers_map.svg/960px-Saint-Barth%C3%A9lemy_quartiers_map.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Le Château, Saint Barthélemy","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":17.906111,"lo":-62.841389,"d":1435,"ds":"Le Château (French pronunciation: [lə ʃato]) is a quartier of Saint Barthélemy in the Caribbean. It is located in the