French pronunciation: [kamaʁyʃ]) is a quartier of Saint Barthélemy in the Caribbean. It is located in the eastern-central part of the island.","wpu":"Camaruche","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Saint-Barth%C3%A9lemy_quartiers_map.svg/960px-Saint-Barth%C3%A9lemy_quartiers_map.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Île Chevreau","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":17.934167,"lo":-62.851389,"d":4132,"ds":"Île Chevreau, also known as Île Bonhomme, is an uninhabited island off the north coast of Saint Barthélemy in the Caribbean. It is a part of the French Antilles, and the westernmost of a series of islands north of Saint Barthélemy. The island is inhabited by a variety of reptiles.","wpu":"Île Chevreau","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Saint_Barth_-_Vue_a%C3%A9rienne_-_Octobre_2009.jpg/960px-Saint_Barth_-_Vue_a%C3%A9rienne_-_Octobre_2009.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Pointe Milou","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":17.915833,"lo":-62.815556,"d":4295,"ds":"Pointe Milou (French pronunciation: [pwɛ̃t milu]) is a quartier of Saint Barthélemy in the Caribbean. It is located in the northeastern part of the island.","wpu":"Pointe Milou","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Saint-Barth%C3%A9lemy_quartiers_map.svg/960px-Saint-Barth%C3%A9lemy_quartiers_map.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Morne Rouge, Saint Barthélemy","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":17.883611,"lo":-62.811389,"d":4448,"ds":"Morne Rouge (French pronunciation: [mɔʁn ʁuʒ]) is a quartier of Saint Barthélemy in the Caribbean. It is located in the southern part of the island.","wpu":"Morne Rouge, Saint Barthélemy","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Saint-Barth%C3%A9lemy_quartiers_map.svg/960px-Saint-Barth%C3%A9lemy_quartiers_map.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Vitet","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":17.903333,"lo":-62.806944,"d":4714,"ds":"Vitet is a quartier of Saint Barthélemy in the Caribbean. It is located in the eastern-central part of the island.","wpu":"Vitet","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Saint-Barth%C3%A9lemy_quartiers_map.svg/960px-Saint-Barth%C3%A9lemy_quartiers_map.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Mont Jean","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":17.915556,"lo":-62.809722,"d":4830,"ds":"Mont Jean (French pronunciation: [mɔ̃ ʒɑ̃]) is a quartier of Saint Barthélemy in the Caribbean. It is located in the northeastern part of the island.","wpu":"Mont Jean","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Saint-Barth%C3%A9lemy_quartiers_map.svg/960px-Saint-Barth%C3%A9lemy_quartiers_map.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Grand Fond","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":17.896667,"lo":-62.804722,"d":4896,"ds":"Grand Fond (French pronunciation: [ɡʁɑ̃ fɔ̃]) is a quartier of Saint Barthélemy in the Caribbean. It is located in the southeastern part of the island.","wpu":"Grand Fond","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Saint-Barth%C3%A9lemy_quartiers_map.svg/960px-Saint-Barth%C3%A9lemy_quartiers_map.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Grand Cul-de-Sac","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":17.908056,"lo":-62.805833,"d":4934,"ds":"Grand Cul-de-Sac (French pronunciation: [ɡʁɑ̃ ky d(ə) sak]) is a quartier of Saint Barthélemy, Caribbean. It is located in the northeastern part of the island.","wpu":"Grand Cul-de-Sac","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Saint-Barth%C3%A9lemy_quartiers_map.svg/960px-Saint-Barth%C3%A9lemy_quartiers_map.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Île Frégate","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":17.939722,"lo":-62.834167,"d":5073,"ds":"Île Frégate is a small, uninhabited island in the Caribbean Sea located off the north coast of Saint Barthélemy, an overseas collectivity of France. Île Frégate is situated within the Nature Reserve of Saint Bartholomew, which was established in 1996 with the objective of conserving coral reefs, sea grass beds and marine life.","wpu":"Île Frégate","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Saint_Barth_-_Vue_a%C3%A9rienne_-_Octobre_2009.jpg/960px-Saint_Barth_-_Vue_a%C3%A9rienne_-_Octobre_2009.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Toiny","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":17.897222,"lo":-62.8,"d":5396,"ds":"Toiny is a quartier of Saint Barthélemy in the Caribbean. It is located in the southeastern part of the island.","wpu":"Toiny","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Saint-Barth%C3%A9lemy_quartiers_map.svg/960px-Saint-Barth%C3%A9lemy_quartiers_map.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Devet, Saint Barthélemy","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":17.901944,"lo":-62.797778,"d":5658,"ds":"Devet is a quartier of Saint Barthélemy in the Caribbean. It is located in the eastern part of the island.","wpu":"Devet, Saint Barthélemy","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Saint-Barth%C3%A9lemy_quartiers_map.svg/960px-Saint-Barth%C3%A9lemy_quartiers_map.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"La Tortue, Saint Barthélemy","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":17.919722,"lo":-62.798056,"d":6145,"ds":"La Tortue ou l'Ecalle, Île Tortue or Turtle Island is a small rocky islet off the north-eastern coast of Saint Barthélemy in the Caribbean. Its highest point is 35 metres (115 ft) above sea level. Referencing tortoises, it forms part of the Réserve naturelle nationale de Saint-Barthélemy with several of the other northern islets of St Barts.","wpu":"La Tortue, Saint Barthélemy","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Saint-Barth%C3%A9lemy_Island_topographic_map-fr.svg/960px-Saint-Barth%C3%A9lemy_Island_topographic_map-fr.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Île Toc Vers","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":17.943056,"lo":-62.816667,"d":6278,"ds":"Île Toc Vers is a small island group off the north coast of Saint Barthélemy in the Caribbean. They are the northeasternmost of a series of islands which include Île Chevreau and Île Frégate. The Île Toc Vers group consists of three small rocky islands, aligned in a north–south fashion, between 15 and 43 metres in height.","wpu":"Île Toc Vers","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Saint_Barth_-_Vue_a%C3%A9rienne_-_Octobre_2009.jpg/960px-Saint_Barth_-_Vue_a%C3%A9rienne_-_Octobre_2009.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Île Fourchue","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":17.958333,"lo":-62.9,"d":8566,"ds":"Île Fourchue, also known as Île Fourche, is an island between Saint-Barthélemy and Saint Martin, belonging to the Collectivity of Saint Barthélemy. The island's inside is privately owned. It is located about 5 km north-west of the island of Saint Barthelemy.","wpu":"Île Fourchue","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/%C3%8Ele_Fourchue.jpg/960px-%C3%8Ele_Fourchue.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Gustavia (, French: [ɡystavja], Swedish: [ɡɵˈstɑːvɪa]) is the main town and capital of the island of Saint Barthélemy. Originally called Le Carénage, it was renamed in honor of King Gustav III of Sweden.","wpu":"Gustavia","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Gustavia_Harbor%2C_Saint-Barth%C3%A9lemy.jpg/960px-Gustavia_Harbor%2C_Saint-Barth%C3%A9lemy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}